2" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(4,0,-1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨2,-6,3⟩.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $PA=7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-77442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨4,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,-6,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OA} & =⟨4,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,-6,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨4,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,-6,3⟩)-⟨4,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨2,-6,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,-6t,\\,3t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=7,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PA & =7 \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =7 \\\\ |⟨2t,\\,-6t,\\,3t⟩| & =7 \\\\ \\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(-6t)^{2}+(3t)^{2}} & =7 \\\\ \\sqrt{49{t}^{2}} & =7 \\\\ \\pm 7t & =7 \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨4,0,-1⟩+⟨2,-6,3⟩=⟨6,-6,2⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨4,0,-1⟩-⟨2,-6,3⟩=⟨2,6,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${A}_{1}(6,-6,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,6,-4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-77442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8129250ff4650a501b248721f22d2c799770249c46ad0e35a73a450d94f5f7de"} {"question" "q-77442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-77442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${A}_{1}(10,2,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,6,-4)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(10,2,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(7,6,-3)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(6,-6,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(10,18,8)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(6,-6,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,6,-4)$"] ["text" "${A}_{1}(8,-12,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(7,6,-3)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-77442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${A}_{1}(6,-6,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,6,-4)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-126458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $C(-1,0,4)$ and $D(-7,2,11).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-126458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $C$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=c+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $c$ is the position vector of $C.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $C(-1,0,4)$ and $D(-7,2,11)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =⟨-7,2,11⟩-⟨-1,0,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,2,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-126458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8129250ff4650a501b248721f22d2c799770249c46ad0e35a73a450d94f5f7de"} {"question" "q-126458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-126458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-126458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-126744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $F(-5,-2,4)$ and $G(3,-1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-126744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $F$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=f+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $f$ is the position vector of $F.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $F(-5,-2,4)$ and $G(3,-1,1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{FG} \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,1⟩-⟨-5,-2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,1,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-126744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8129250ff4650a501b248721f22d2c799770249c46ad0e35a73a450d94f5f7de"} {"question" "q-126744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-126744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-126744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-162161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation below describes all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(3,0,-2)$ and $Q(1,1,-1).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ b \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [c,1]\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-162161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand the vector equation of the  line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=3+1+0=4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-162161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8129250ff4650a501b248721f22d2c799770249c46ad0e35a73a450d94f5f7de"} {"question" "q-162161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-162161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-162161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-162173" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation below gives a parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(3,2,-1)$ and $Q(0,1,-3).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=a\\,i+b\\,j-(2t+1)\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,c]\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-162173" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(j-3\\,k)-(3\\,i+2\\,j-k) \\\\  & =-3\\,i-j-2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=(3\\,i+2\\,j-k)+t(-3\\,i-j-2\\,k)\n$$\n\nand the parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(3\\,i+2\\,j-k)+t(-3\\,i-j-2\\,k) \\\\  & =(3-3t)\\,i+(2-t)\\,j-(2t+1)\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,1].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=(3-3t)+(2-t)+1=6-4t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-162173" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8129250ff4650a501b248721f22d2c799770249c46ad0e35a73a450d94f5f7de"} {"question" "q-162173" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-162173" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2t-1"] ["math" "3t"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6-4t"] ["math" "t+5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082381/state.json" "file_sha256" "10d7ac25db77f8310a0d088a7b1ed5bdea772490476c2410fde2f8fce608cd60"} {"question" "q-162173" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6-4t"] "category" "m